4. Difference between Runnable and Callable?
Callable return a result and can throw an exception, it is suitable like api calls.
Runnable doesn't return a result and can't throw an exception, it is suitable for side effects, like logging.

5. What is the difference between t.start() and t.run()?
t.start() starts a new thread and run in a separate thread, it can run multiple threads concurrently. t.run()
run in the current thread and run threads sequentially.

6. Which way of creating threads is better: Thread class or Runnable interface
Runnable interface is betters. Because Java only support single inheritance of class, so if we extend thread
class, we can't inherit another class, which may cause some problems for our application logics. The code is
less flexible than implementing Runnable interface. And runnable interface is better with thread pooling,
like executorService.

