10. What’s the difference between class lock and object lock?
Class lock applies to the entire class, ensuring thread safe for static methods. Object lock is for an
instance, ensuring thread safe for instance methods.

11. What is join() method?
Pause the current thread until the join thread complete.

12. what is yield() method?
Pause the current thread to give a change the the same or higher priority thread to run. It doesn't
guarantee the thread order, but just tell cpu that current thread can yield.

13. What is ThreadPool? How many types of ThreadPool? What is the TaskQueue in ThreadPool?
Thread pool is a pool of reusable threads to efficiently manage tasks. The thread pool maintains a fixed
number of threads that can be reused. We have FixedThreadPool, CachedThreadPool, SingleThreadExecutor.
TaskQueue is a queue of tasks waiting to be executed.

