16. What is the advantage of ThreadPool?
First we can reuse threads so better performance and minimal overhead. It simplify the thread management
process so less manual work compared to traditional thread management. It helps manage tasks efficiently
as FIFO order.

17. Difference between shutdown() and shutdownNow() methods of executor
Shutdown means don't accept new tasks but will not stop the running tasks. But shutdownNow() will stop
the running tasks.

18. What is Atomic classes? How many types of Atomic classes? Give me some code example of Atomic
classes and its main methods. when to use it?
Atomic classes make thread safe without using a lock. We have AtomicInteger, AtomicLong, AtomicBoolean.
addAndGet(), incrementAndGet(), getAndSet(), getAndIncrement(). It is good for simple counters.

19. What kind of locks do you know? What is the advantage of each lock?
Intrinsic lock: object lock/class lock with synchronized keyword, easy to implement, good for simple tasks.
Explicit lock: ReentrantLock, lock.lock(): obtain locks, lock.unlock(): release locks, and we need to
consider about exception. ReadWriteLock, we cannot write while read. StampedLock: we can write while read
but need to handle thread safety issue.

